# Infrastructure Investment Business Case — Q3 FY26
**Document type:** Business case / financial model
**Classification:** Confidential
**Author:** Finance & Strategy Team
**Date:** April 2026

---

## Executive Summary

This document presents the business case for Acme Corp's Q3 FY26 infrastructure modernization initiative. The proposed investment of $12.4M in cloud infrastructure migration and on-premises hardware refresh is projected to generate an NPV of $4.2M over a 5-year horizon at the CFO-mandated discount rate of 8.5%.

## Investment Scope

- Cloud migration: $7.2M (Years 1–2)
- On-premises hardware refresh: $3.1M (Year 1)
- Professional services and training: $1.4M (Year 1)
- Contingency reserve (10%): $0.7M

## 5-Year Cash Flow Projections

| Year | CapEx ($M) | OpEx Savings ($M) | Revenue Enablement ($M) | Net Cash Flow ($M) |
|------|-----------|-------------------|--------------------------|-------------------|
| Y1   | -12.4      | 0.3               | 0.0                      | -12.1              |
| Y2   | -0.5       | 1.8               | 0.5                      | 1.8                |
| Y3   | 0.0        | 2.4               | 1.2                      | 3.6                |
| Y4   | 0.0        | 2.4               | 2.0                      | 4.4                |
| Y5   | 0.0        | 2.4               | 2.5                      | 4.9                |

## NPV Calculation

Discount rate: 8.5% (per CFO Q3 guidance memo)
IRR: 14.2%
Payback period: 3.4 years
NPV (5-year, 8.5% discount): **$4.2M**

## Risk Assumptions

- Migration risk: Medium. Contingency covers up to 15% cost overrun.
- Vendor lock-in: Mitigated by multi-cloud architecture.
- Timeline risk: 6-month delay scenario reduces NPV by $0.9M (still positive).

## Recommendation

Proceed with the infrastructure investment. All financial hurdles are met at the CFO-specified discount rate. Board approval memo from Q2 FY26 covers the required capital envelope.
